※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4371
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4371 LANG_RELRO_NOT_AT_TOP_LEVEL

※ `@[relro]` stands only on a variable at the top level.  What it promises is
※ about the life of the program -- the constructors run, the pages are made
※ read-only, the startup function runs -- and a variable inside a function is
※ made and gone within one call, with no moment in its life the promise is
※ about.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    @[relro]
    let count: mut u8 = 1u8
    count ← count + 1u8
    ⎕narrow(count, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 0u6
